6. Allowed “moves” between the layers
The ordered way of jumping also comes with legal transformations.
Resolution graph moves
On the graph side:
blow-up;
blow-down;
add exceptional vertex;
contract (−1)(-1)(−1)-curves when legal;
change weights;
refine intersections.
On the singularity side:
resolution;
partial resolution;
deformation;
smoothing;
contraction;
plumbing.
These correspond roughly as:
blow-up in geometry↔local graph refinement\text{blow-up in geometry}
